From 1320cd441d1368e21288f4cc76d7533c2a500703 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jordi <jordi@exante.ai>
Date: Mon, 8 Jun 2026 16:28:16 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(app): work-driven zones, spawn-walk, and grounded
 floors
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Zones now reflect real work: the daemon classifies the tool in use into a
  local work-kind (read/edit/run/web) served via /sessions; the compositor maps
  it to both the diorama zone and the pet's action (read→mine, edit→chop wood,
  run→gather, web→fish at the pond). A category only — no prompt/code text leaves
  the machine.
- Spawn-walk: a newly spawned pet runs in from the player's cell down to its own
  tile, then settles into work (renderer ticker; floor/prop wait at the tile).
- Grounded floors: the ground is now a repeating TilingSprite pad with a soft
  contact shadow under each pet; fixed the distorted grove tile crop.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
